mlsbD0ibm9uZSIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj4KPHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjI0IiBoZWlnaHQ9IjI0IiBmaWxsPSIjRkZGRkZGIi8+Cjwvc3ZnPgo=\"/>\n<div class=\"text\">\n<div class=\"title\">Specification</div>\n<div class=\"desc\">Essential electrical and physical parameters.</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<a class=\"download-btn\" href=\"https://store.bblcdn.com/s1/default/42e9a3a1a12e423b9f4041fdb1eb1756/Multi-Function_Controller_Core_(1PCS)_-_XA003.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Download</a></div>\n<div class=\"doc-item\">\n<div class=\"doc-info\"><img alt=\"Solid Model\" class=\"icon-img product-desc-lazy-media product-desc-lazy-media--image bg-bbl-white animate-pulse max-h-[400px]\" data-lazy=\"false\" data-src=\"https://store.bblcdn.com/s1/default/c09f0bcff3184a679d3beb705f2ddd6f/Download.png\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMjQiIGhlaWdodD0iMjQiIHZpZXdCb3g9IjAgMCAyNCAyNCIgZmlsbD0ibm9uZSIgeG1sbnM9Imh0dHA6Ly93d3cudzMub3JnLzIwMDAvc3ZnIj4KPHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjI0IiBoZWlnaHQ9IjI0IiBmaWxsPSIjRkZGRkZGIi8+Cjwvc3ZnPgo=\"/>\n<div class=\"text\">\n<div class=\"title\">Solid Model</div>\n<div class=\"desc\">3D model of structure and dimensions.</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<a class=\"download-btn\" href=\"https://store.bblcdn.com/s1/default/383aa529f7d24117b9b0355e6780066c/Multi-Function_Controller_Core_3D_Model-XA003.zip\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Download</a></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"pct pct_mc\">\n<div class=\"pct_t-icpc\">\n<h2 class=\"pct_t\" style=\"font-size: 24px; text-align: center;\">Important Notices</h2>\n<p></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">For security and stability, the CyberBrick Multi-Function Core Board only supports firmware updates through official tools. Flashing with third-party tools is not supported and may cause irreversible damage, which is not covered by warranty. Please use only official tools for any firmware operations. Thank you for your understanding!</li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">If you have purchased the time-lapse photography shield and are using it together with the Cyberbrick core board, <span style=\"color: #00ae42;\"><a href=\"https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/cyberbrick/troubleshooting/wired-firmware-guide\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"color: #00ae42;\" target=\"_blank\">please refer to the wiki to flash the time-lapse photography firmware.</a></span></li>\n<li style=\"text-align: left; font-size: 16px;\">The company is not responsible for any device damage, malfunction, fire, or other losses resulting from failure to comply with the above requirements. Please strictly follow the safety instructions for this product.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
  "description_text": "You can pair this product with either the Remote Control Receiver Shield or the Remote Control Transmitter Shield to serve as the receiver or transmitter component in RC projects. Additionally, by combining it with the Time-lapse Expansion Board, you can create a time-lapse photography module for Bambu Lab 3D printers.\n\nExplore the Product Wiki & Documentation Need in-depth assembly guides, troubleshooting, or technical details for this product? Visit our official Wiki to discover comprehensive resources and answers to all your questions. Visit Wiki\n\nExplore the Product Wiki & Documentation Need in-depth assembly guides, troubleshooting, or technical details for this product? Visit our official Wiki to discover comprehensive resources and answers to all your questions.\n\nExplore the Product Wiki & Documentation\n\nNeed in-depth assembly guides, troubleshooting, or technical details for this product? Visit our official Wiki to discover comprehensive resources and answers to all your questions.\n\nVisit Wiki\n\nFor security and stability, the CyberBrick Multi-Function Core Board only supports firmware updates through official tools. Flashing with third-party tools is not supported and may cause irreversible damage, which is not covered by warranty. Please use only official tools for any firmware operations. Thank you for your understanding!\n\nIf you have purchased the time-lapse photography shield and are using it together with the Cyberbrick core board, please refer to the wiki to flash the time-lapse photography firmware.\n\nThe company is not responsible for any device damage, malfunction, fire, or other losses resulting from failure to comply with the above requirements. Please strictly follow the safety instructions for this product.",
